<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacques Dyel du Parquet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1606">1606</a>–<a href="/years/1658">1658</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacques Dyel du Parquet was a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-belain-desnambuc">Pierre Belain d'Esnambuc</a> and governor of Martinique from 1637. In 1649 he landed settlers on Grenada and built a fort at the site of St George's, and in 1650 he sent settlers to Saint Lucia. That year he bought Martinique, Grenada and Saint Lucia from the bankrupt Company of the Isles of America, ruling them as proprietor until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacques-dyel-du-parquet.jpg" alt="Jacques Dyel du Parquet" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dyel_du_Parquet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
